course: dictionary
lesson: 5847
title: Malayan: a word about a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Malayan is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you more about a noun, such as which frog or which tiger. «The Malayan leaf frog is brown and flat» tells us which frog we mean: the one from the Malayan region.
explain: The context clues show where the word points. The frog is brown and flat, so it blends in with dead leaves on the floor. Malayan links it to the Malay Peninsula, where it lives.
explain: Malayan can also be a noun, a name for a person from Malaya. This is an old-fashioned use. When Malayan comes straight before a noun like frog or tiger, it is an adjective.
fact: Malayan means to do with Malaya, the old name for the land on the Malay Peninsula.
fact: Malaya later became part of Malaysia. It was a British colony, became independent in 1957 and joined Malaysia in 1963.
fact: Animals with Malayan in their name, such as the Malayan tiger, Malayan tapir and Malayan sun bear, are found in the Malay Peninsula region.
fact: Malayan tigers and Malayan tapirs are endangered, which means they are at risk of dying out.
fact: In old use, a Malayan is a person from Malaya.
exercise: «The Malayan leaf frog is brown and flat.» What kind of word is Malayan here? | A word for a colour | A word for an action | A name for a person | *A describing word that tells us which frog
exercise: Ella says, «The Malayan tiger lives in the jungle.» Where do Malayan animals come from? | The deserts of Australia | *The Malay Peninsula region | The cold mountains of Scotland
exercise: In old use, what is «a Malayan»? | A king who lived long ago | A kind of tiger | A type of boat | *A person from Malaya
test: Which name is the old name for the land on the Malay Peninsula? | *Malaya | Malta | Malawi | Madagascar
test: In which year did Malaya join Malaysia? | *1963 | 1970 | 1945 | 1957
exam: In the sentence «The Malayan sun bear climbs tall trees», where is this bear found? | On the coast of Peru | *In the Malay Peninsula region | In the Sahara desert | In Iceland
